# Gate step 1352-vmbc — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq).
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS. `./build.sh --preflight` is the front door: the step every PR
# runs before `gh pr ready`, and the one that catches a sub-second decider an
# author never ran. It launched every guard under `setsid` unconditionally, and
# `setsid` is util-linux.
#
# MEASURED ON macOS BEFORE THE FIX:
#     ./build.sh: line 316: exec: setsid: not found
#     refused:preflight:ran=0 skipped=3 failed=108 wall=26s
# ran=0. Not "some deciders red" — NONE of the 108 launched, and 108 identical
# launch failures are indistinguishable, in the summary line, from 108 real
# refusals about the tree. AFTER: ran=94 skipped=16 failed=1
# isolation=none-no-setsid.
#
# IT FAILED LOUD RATHER THAN GREEN, which bounded the damage — a mac got
# `refused`, never a false pass — and is why this was a blocked host rather than
# a fleet of quietly unverified pushes. What it could not do was say anything
# about the tree.
#
# THE TREE ALREADY KNEW THIS PLATFORM LACKS setsid, which is what made it a
# defect rather than a platform limit: scripts/test-dispatch-reap.sh:99 probes
# `command -v setsid` and emits a named skip under 1141-vf9w ("NOT the same as
# passing"). One caller asked and one did not.
#
# THE FIX IS THE PROBE, NEVER THE DROP. build.sh's own comment above
# _pf_run_guard records what was measured without setsid: `timeout N cmd` does
# not reliably reach cmd's children, one door run left NINE survivors including
# the timeout processes themselves, and setsid's exit propagation broke the 124
# detection so two timed-out guards were reported as refusals rather than skips.
# Arm 4 of the fixture pins that comment for the next reader who is tempted.
#
# WHY THE VERDICT NAMES THE MODE. A run without setsid keeps every deadline and
# the 124 convention and loses only process-GROUP signalling, so a guard that
# leaves background children can outlive its deadline. That is a real difference
# in what the run PROVED. A degraded run that reads like an isolated one is
# worse than a refusal, so both summary lines carry `isolation=`, and the
# fixture's arm 3 requires BOTH — pinning only the refusal line would let a
# green run hide a degraded one, which is the direction that costs something.
#
# WHAT THIS STEP RUNS is a source-shape fixture, and that is a deliberate
# limitation rather than a shortcut: the behavioural proof is a 150s preflight
# run, which is the one thing a front-door step cannot be. The before/after pair
# above is recorded on the row as the measurement; this step pins that the three
# pieces producing it cannot be removed silently.
#
# STEP_SCRIPT is a LITERAL path on purpose: a binding assembled from a variable
# is invisible to every name-based scan (1063-nraf).
# SECOND REGIME (order 1302-7j8p / macneo's checker). RUN ON THE REGIME, not
# inferred from it: the four arms below were executed on darwin, on the host that
# produced this row's evidence, and the verdict recorded is the fixture's own
# output — not a claim about --preflight's summary, which is a different
# measurement and belongs on the row.
#
# This step is the one case where the darwin run is not a courtesy: the defect it
# guards EXISTS ONLY on a host without setsid, so a Linux-only attestation would
# be an attestation from the regime that cannot reproduce the bug.
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="tlatoanis-macbook-air 2026-09-22 darwin ok:preflight-setsid-probe:4"

STEP_DESC="Checking the preflight probes for setsid and names its isolation mode (1352-vmbc)"
STEP_SCRIPT="scripts/test-preflight-setsid-probe.sh"
STEP_ERROR="the preflight's setsid probe or its isolation-mode verdict was removed (1352-vmbc) — without the probe, every guard on a host with no setsid dies in its exec and the step reports ran=0; without the verdict token, a degraded run reads as an isolated one. Do NOT 'fix' by deleting setsid: build.sh's own comment records nine survivors and broken 124 detection from the run that tried"
STEP_OK="The preflight runs its guards on a host without setsid, and says so"
